Z||000000||zeusrekning||12-14-2000||07:17 PM||||I just bought an 88 coupe and it dosen't have the take off power my 87 has. The motor in my 87 is about shot and i hate to loose it cause it has a lot more power.I have always felt my 87 has been rebuilt and modified. I gues i should check compression. What else?<BR>Thanks||||reg||2
Z||000001||Tom88gt||12-14-2000||07:21 PM||||I assume they are both the same engines.  L4 or V-6?  If they are the same and one has a lot less power, it may just need a tune up.  Check all the cheap basics first (timing, plugs, air filter, vac hoses, etc) before you assume bigger $$$ problems.||||reg||1
Z||000002||zeusrekning||12-14-2000||07:30 PM||||yeah both are 4cyl. There is a big diff.<BR>allways heard the 4cyl sucked but i never thought mine did. Need someone to come over and drive it. The only gt i have drove was an auto 86 and it felt just like mine.<BR>Mine in a 5speed though.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||12-14-2000||07:39 PM||||See what transmission options are in them both. That would effect power.<P>you'll need to go thru the 88 and look for problems after that. Read my DIS and Torque strut articles. Check the base of the TBI very carefully. If the dog bone is letting the air cleaner hit the trunk then the TBI may have a vacuum leak.||||reg||1
Z||000004||zeusrekning||12-14-2000||07:42 PM||||Transmisson feels great. I was thinking the t-body. So the 2.5 isn't really all that weak?||||reg||1
Z||000005||WKDFIRO||12-15-2000||05:28 AM||||In 1988 the Iron Duke was fitted with counter rotating shafts supposedly to smooth out vibrations. Thats why you won't find the oil filter sticking out of the side of the block like you do on the 87. I never felt any differences in vibration in either my 87 (even with urethane dog bone) or the 88. <P>I don't beleive that the 88 4 cyl were any weaker than the 87, but different engines with different owners will act differently depending on how easy or rough a life they have gone through. My 87 manual and the 87 automatic were both pretty good offline. What are the differences in mileage?<P>||||reg||2
Z||000006||zeusrekning||12-15-2000||06:19 AM||||My 87 has 225,000 miles and the 88 has 133,000.The more I think about it the more i feel there is something wrong. Just because the car is super clean and tranny feels great. Mabey something happened and the power loss made the owner get rid of it.<BR>????????????????<BR>yes I'm trying to get my hopes up.||||reg||1
Z||000007||ChadMan||12-15-2000||09:13 AM||||Maybe the 88 Duke really is weaker.<P>Dale2M4 and I were at Mid-Ohio this summer doing (ahem) parade laps.  The guys in front of us took off, so naturally we had to try and keep pace.  Dale and I ran flat-out down the first half of the back straight before we caught up to traffic and had to slow down.  He was slowly and steadily pulling away from me in his 87 Coupe.  He even had 150 lbs of extra weight in his car! (A/C + his son)<P>Surely the balance shafts wouldn't sap more than one hp or so?||||reg||5
Z||000008||theogre||12-15-2000||11:03 AM||||To the best f my knowlege the entire top half of the motors is the same. <P>The only dif in the block may be added metal for the ballance to bolt to. I say may be because I believe the ballance assebly bolts up in place of 2 main caps. Obviously the crank has the balance drive gear on it.<P>I'd go thru it and look at all the usual stuff. Vac leaks, plugs & wires, all that junk. I can't imagine there's a huge diferance in the motors that would cause this.<P>I said check the tranny RPO's because they may have differant final gears. This would make the cars have diferant percieved engine poer.<P>As far as the 2.5 being weak I'm still looking into the 110hp rating GM gave them in 89-90. I have a feeling that the 87-88 ones may have been intentionally under rated at 98hp. GM has done that many times in the past.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 12-15-2000).]||||reg||1
